From df13a549aae46085ee937caf420628c46a3c35ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: spotUP <retroranksmail@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 21:19:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 04/12] gh-127545: Specify minimum PyGC_Head and PyObject
 alignment (backport)

Backport of python/cpython#135209 (merged to main for 3.15; the 3.13 and
3.14 backport labels were dropped). The GC keeps flags in the low two
bits of _gc_prev and PyStackRef tags live in the low bits of object
pointers; m68k's ABI aligns these structs to 2 bytes, which crashes
_bootstrap_python (Debian m68k). Applied unchanged from
https://github.com/python/cpython/pull/135209.diff.

Original author: Finn Thain <fthain@linux-m68k.org>

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
